      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pivot toward restorative justice is a necessary response to the crisis of legitimacy in the criminal justice system, as it acknowledges the failures of the traditional retributive model and seeks to address the root causes of social unrest. By prioritizing rehabilitation, reparation, and community healing, restorative justice offers a more nuanced and effective approach to justice that recognizes the harm caused by crime and seeks to repair it. This shift is not a distraction from the core function of punishment, but rather a necessary evolution of the justice system to ensure it remains relevant and effective in promoting social cohesion and trust.",
      "source": "target",
